WEBVTT

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:10.270
Play your dream for me.
Kanadete yume

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:20.140
Rental Magica

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:28.120
The shadow of the moon as it waxes and wanes...
Michikakeru tsuki no kage sotto

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:37.800
...gently stirs the beat of sorrow in your heart.
kanashimi no kodou furuwasu

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:42.490
Its wandering attraction...
Samayou inryoku

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.430
...reflected in your eyes.
hitomi ni utsushite

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:53.420
You will surpass the darkness of Ioneliness.
Kodoku no yami wo koeteyuku

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:59.120
You know that truth in your heart.
Shinjitsu wa kono mune ni

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:04.790
That gentleness will become your strength.
Yasashisa wa tsuyosa ni naru

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:09.430
Don't be afraid. Believe.
Osorenaide shinjiru koto

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:14.270
The brilliance that blooms in the cosmos eternally...
Sora ni saku kirameki wa towa ni

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.240
...embraces the voice of time.
toki no koe dakishime

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:24.310
Play your dream for me.
Kanadete yume

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:29.050
Let me hear.
Kikasete

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:33.780
Wind, speak to me.
Kaze tsutaete

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:40.290
Tell me what courage is.
Yuuki wo

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.070
As I thought.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:56.300
I fear the city will change again tonight.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.240
I won't let it happen this time!

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.780
Who... am I?

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.170
Episode 22
THE SLEEPING CITY

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:28.670
I've never tasted anything like it.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.370
R-Really?

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.770
Oh, may I have an extra helping of ramen?

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.480
And some marinated pork belly as well, please.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.240
Huh?!

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:42.520
Sure...

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:49.330
If you'd said you only like
high-class restaurants,

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.000
I don't know what I would have done.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.990
The flavor of a meal depends as much
on the company as it does on the food.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:57.130
Huh?

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.570
R-Right...

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.680
It was here, wasn't it.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.780
The place where we first met.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.110
You came riding in on a demon.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.080
I thought I was going to die.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:12.950
You're exaggerating.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.090
This was also where I had
my reunion with Honami.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:22.260
I've always wondered why
Honami came to Astral.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.900
Even without choosing us,

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:30.560
she would have been in demand with all
sorts of magical organizations, wouldn't she?

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:36.140
Honami was always alone,
always in some sort of rush to learn magic.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.500
Reviving the nearly extinct magic of the Celts...

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.240
Normally, even a genius would have
required a lifetime to do that.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.520
She did it at that young an age.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:52.060
The word talent doesn't begin to cover
her extraordinary level of passion.

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:55.860
I wonder where she got such
strong feelings about it?

00:03:56.200 --> 00:04:00.130
She went straight to Astral
right after graduation.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:00.760
Huh?

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:05.400
Perhaps she had made a promise to someone.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:08.780
Or perhaps it's even more uncertain.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:11.440
A vow that she secretly made in her heart.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:13.580
A vow...

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:20.410
That's something you'll need to
know some day, isn't it, Itsuki?

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:23.280
Yeah...

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.730
Jeez, it's just the two of us,

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.660
and we end up talking about Honami.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.190
It's like a dream.

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:36.370
Someone like me, enrolled in a regular school,

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:39.530
taking regular exams, eating ramen.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.310
Oh?

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.970
That sort of stuff is like a dream to you?

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:48.610
Yeah, like a dream.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.420
Itsuki, thank you.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:54.620
Y-You have nothing to thank me for.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.120
Excuse me!

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:02.130
Somebody, help me, please!

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.430
Um, excuse me! You, over there!

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.910
I came up here to catch this little one...

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.900
...and now I can't get down.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.870
Could you catch him?

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:16.770
Uh, sure.

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:26.150
Sorry, looks like I interrupted something.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.380
You didn't interrupt anything.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:30.920
Thanks.

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:34.890
My name's Fin Cruda.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.960
Oh, no. I should thank you, too.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.670
This cat belongs to my company.

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:46.070
Company?

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:47.700
Um, well...

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:51.150
Mage Recruiting Agency
ASTRAL
We rent mages to meet your demands.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.050
Mage Recruiting Agency
ASTRAL
We rent mages to meet your demands.
How can I ever thank you?

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.180
You saved Genbu's life.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.920
Sorry to impose on you like this,

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.290
but when Itsuki mentioned your company,

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:02.480
I was interested in seeing it.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:05.420
Nekoyashiki seems to have
these as a reward for you.

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:07.860
I got them from someone else,
but please help yourself.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.230
Wow!

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:12.770
I love crème puffs!

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:15.530
I'm glad. Please, take as much as you like.

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:16.860
Delicious!

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:23.570
The custard's great,
and the crust is nice and crisp.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:24.110
We're back.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:24.780
We're back.
We're back.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:25.250
We're back.

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:26.740
Thank you, Honami.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.440
Oh? Where have you two been?

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:35.250
I had disaster drill at school today,
so Big Sister Honami came to get me.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:40.020
Fin?!

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.030
It's been a while... Honami.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.150
Huh?

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.130
What are you doing here?

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.160
Is he an acquaintance of yours, Honami?

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.830
Um, more like my senior than an acquaintance.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:56.840
He let me study Celtic magic with him.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:00.170
Huh? Then you're a mage too?

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.450
Forgive me for not having mentioned it.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:07.880
So, I spotted that girl over
there a while ago, too.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.720
Um, hi.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:13.120
What brings you here today?

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:14.990
The truth is,

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:18.430
I'm here as an agent of The Association.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.900
You're saying our president committed a taboo?!

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:25.770
What do you mean?

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:28.640
Y... Yeah, what's this all about?

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:34.280
It's just a suspicion right now.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:38.370
That's why I've been sent here as an observer.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:45.920
Taboos are when mages break rules
that must never be broken, right?

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:49.090
There's no way Brother Pres would do that!

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:53.760
Um, first of all, I'm not even a mage.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.440
That is to say,

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:57.130
what taboo is he accused of breaking?

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:00.070
That still isn't clear.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:05.570
The word from The Association is that
Astral is hiding some sort of major secret.

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:10.450
Itsuki's taboo seems to be connected with it.

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:13.120
I don't really see your point.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:14.850
Nekoyashiki,

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.160
as one of Astral's oldest members,

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.180
wouldn't you know something about this?

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.830
And if I say... I don't?

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:27.860
That doesn't matter.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:32.270
Even so, my instincts tell me to trust Astral.

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:35.210
Why would you think that?

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:37.100
Well...

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.710
Because Honami is part of your society.

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:41.910
F-Fin?!

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:51.680
Nekoyashiki, what is this secret that Astral has?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:55.160
Sorry, I couldn't even guess.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.460
Really?

00:08:56.530 --> 00:09:00.370
The way you acted before,
I was sure you knew something.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:05.660
I went along with him to see if
that kid would reveal any faults.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:09.100
He doesn't seem like such a bad person.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:11.340
That's right.

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:14.280
Even though he was sent by
The Association to observe us,

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.250
he said he trusted us because
Honami was in the company.

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:19.520
Big Sister Honami?

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:20.760
Tell us!

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:21.520
What?

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:23.320
What's your relationship with him?

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:26.730
Senior-junior, like I said.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:28.860
What kind of senior-junior relationship?

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.060
Where do you know him from?

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:31.590
The magic school, right?

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:37.830
I met him when I was doing field work here
and there while studying Celtic magic.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:42.680
Honestly, he's more of a very
helpful teacher than just my senior.

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:43.770
Oh?

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:47.480
So, you mean he's a really
amazing mage as well?

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:51.820
He's a bit odd, even for a mage...

00:09:58.330 --> 00:09:59.760
That's strange.

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:01.820
I was sure it was this tree.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.540
My mistletoe!

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.640
Hey, come on!

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:20.470
Can't you wake up?! Wake up!

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:28.180
What's wrong?

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.850
Um, that mistletoe...

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:33.790
I planted and grew it here myself.

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:34.630
Please give it back.

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:35.890
Forgive me.

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:43.600
Weren't you leaving yourself to open to attack?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:46.900
Shouldn't a mage cast a barrier or two?

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:51.010
That mistletoe may have been raised by someone,

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:54.180
but the purity of its spell power
is as good as what grows in the wild.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:11:00.210
I wanted to meet the witch who
could raise such mistletoe.

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:06.160
Now that I think of it,

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:10.190
doesn't Big Brother Fin look like Brother Pres?

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.130
Oh, I thought so as well.

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:14.740
Y... You think?

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:18.210
Yeah. He's sort of aloof
with a calmness about him.

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:20.140
Hm? Where did the president go?

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.280
Wait!

00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:27.580
Wait up!

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:30.210
What's wrong?

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:33.710
There's something I want to ask you, Fin.

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:36.050
Sure.

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.590
Um, well...

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:43.890
Go on.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:47.830
There's a ton of stuff I'd like to ask,

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.130
but I don't know how to put it.

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:56.000
You see, I don't know exactly what a mage is.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:59.740
A mage is a heretical freak.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:04.210
One who explores the limits of those
heresies to become the king of truth.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:09.990
There are some who lead the way
by struggling for knowledge,

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:12.550
mercilessly fending off those who follow them.

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:15.020
There are some who think that.

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:20.730
So long as one is a mage,
they cannot avoid heresy.

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:24.630
But you have it even worse, don't you?

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:28.480
The Glam Sight phenomenon...

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.910
...lets you see deep, hidden places in others.

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:41.510
You can't say that brings
you happiness, can you?

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:48.320
Not to mention how you live in the world
between mages and the mundane.

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:53.790
That eye clearly reveals heresies
and abnormalities to you.

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:59.530
Most of what your eye has seen has
been the failures in others, hasn't it?

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:06.940
But despite that, that needn't be your fate.

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:14.220
What sort of president do you want to be, Itsuki?

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:16.690
Huh? What do you?

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:22.260
I will be who I will be.

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:27.740
I talked big before,

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:30.230
but part of me is still hesitant.

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:33.800
Lame, huh?

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:36.310
This is a nice city.

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:40.710
The flow of the wind, the water,
and the people isn't stagnant.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.620
Even though this is a gathering spot
for ley lines and power nodes,

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:48.250
the city lives with a power of
its own, in spite of them.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:54.420
I can see why Tsukasa Iba, the previous
president, established Astral here.

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:58.630
Setting up Astral in a city like this...

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:01.400
...showed that this is how he wanted to live.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:03.770
How he wanted to live?

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:05.200
Yes.

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:08.910
He was grasping for a way
to live on his own terms,

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:11.710
not content to flow around the outside.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:13.600
So, Itsuki...

00:14:14.380 --> 00:14:15.580
Believe in yourself.

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:17.220
Call yourself president.

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:23.990
Become strong.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:27.820
Um... Thank you.

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:31.100
You've made me feel a lot better.

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:36.660
Maybe because Honami told
me so much about you.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:41.000
She'd be angry if I couldn't
be a little helpful to you.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:48.080
What's wrong?

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:50.840
I... I'm fine.

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:54.920
You should go home early and rest.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:56.780
Yeah...

00:14:58.190 --> 00:14:59.490
I'll do that.

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:02.420
Will you be okay by yourself?

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:05.660
Yeah. I've gotten used to it.

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:12.660
Could you land for a second?

00:15:13.110 --> 00:15:14.130
You noticed me?

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:17.730
You two seemed to be talking about something,

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:19.440
but I couldn't hear what.

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:25.810
I'd better go to the president.

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:28.390
About Itsuki's Glam Sight...

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.990
Why have you hidden it from me until now?

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:38.390
Because... It's my fault Icchan got that eye.

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:41.360
And you knew I knew something about it.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:44.540
That's what you were thinking...

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:47.130
...when you asked to study with me, wasn't it?

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.610
It's not that I was hiding it.

00:15:52.110 --> 00:15:54.650
I just... couldn't tell you.

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:57.810
What was it that Itsuki saw
in this city so long ago?

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.220
Icchan?

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:12.090
NO!!!

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:21.500
There's an impurity lurking in his
eye which cannot be hidden.

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:26.270
It's because he saw this city's secret, isn't it?

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.680
Have you never noticed it?

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:31.610
This city's malaise?

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:39.530
Ever since Itsuki became president,

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:43.360
it's been slowly advancing
somewhere in this city.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:50.100
I'm afraid it's happened whenever
he's used his Glam Sight.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:52.840
Is that what The Association
considers his taboo?

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:54.270
However,

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:57.410
there may be an unexpected twist...

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:59.850
...which can lead to a cure for his eye.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:02.540
Cure... Icchan's?

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:04.910
You can cure Icchan's eye?

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:07.480
What did Itsuki see?

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:12.220
Tell me, Honami.

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:15.620
It was...

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:18.750
...a dragon's egg.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:27.700
That day, Icchan saw a fragment of
a dragon that sleeps in this city.

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:31.370
Where am I?

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:34.170
I've found it.

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:37.650
Who am I?

00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:49.900
Look! Look! Look!

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:51.960
Stop it!!

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:01.670
No good here, either.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.680
And the cell phone isn't getting through.

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:06.740
Do you think Itsuki and Honami are all right?

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:10.050
We may have been slightly outmaneuvered.

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:11.010
Huh?

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:13.020
Now that this has happened,

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:17.150
it looks like I also need to tell
you two about the dragon.

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:23.420
Young Master!

00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:29.700
Sekiren!

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:33.500
Up to your usual cheap tricks, I see.

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:34.980
Well, not surprising,

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:37.030
seeing as how you just hatched.

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:39.780
Indaraya sowaka!

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:48.710
Are you all right?

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:50.360
I think so.

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:52.090
Except my right eye is a little...

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:53.890
That eye patch!

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:01.400
Om shuri mari mamari mari shuri sowaka!

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:10.110
What was that about just now?!

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:13.740
All of the eye patch's function
has been destroyed.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:17.280
Use this for now.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:23.020
That eye patch offers no barrier at all now.

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:34.470
The entire city is asleep.

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:39.240
Why did father choose this city?

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:45.370
Do you think something approaching
a taboo exists in this city, Miss?

00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:47.040
Yes.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:50.880
If that's the reason Astral chose
to establish itself here, then...

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:53.320
Could it be Itsuki?

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:56.450
Daphne, I leave the mansion
in your hands tonight.

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:57.390
Miss!

00:19:57.790 --> 00:19:58.880
Come forth, Forneus!

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:01.360
The marquis who rules 29 legions!

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:13.140
For tonight only,

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:15.440
there's no need to hide you from the public.

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:17.930
The city is asleep?

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:20.780
That how it's hatched this time around.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:25.250
Somebody has been destroying
the seals we once cast...

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.780
to seal up the dragon, one by one.

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:31.190
If we don't settle this tonight, people will die.

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:31.950
Die?!

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:34.920
You've carried too great
a burden, Young Master.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:36.490
I'll cast a barrier.

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:39.990
Please hide here quietly until things settle down.

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:41.260
But, I!

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:45.170
Even so, your eye patch, and the seals...

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:48.610
A mage of great power must be doing this.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:50.140
A mage?

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:52.510
Do you have an idea of who it is?

00:20:53.010 --> 00:20:55.140
Young Master! The city's dangerous!

00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:01.110
It can't be...

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:11.100
Honami, you know where the
dragon is going to incarnate.

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:15.700
Because you've had a path open with it...

00:21:15.700 --> 00:21:17.930
...since the day you and the dragon met.

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:22.670
His Glam Sight is being warped
by terrific spell power.

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:29.180
It would be nearly impossible for even an
expert mage to wipe away the impurity itself.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:32.350
But a dragon is an entirely different matter.

00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:35.580
Icchan's eye can be cured.

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:43.660
Icchan's eye can be cured...

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:07.880
Over and over, holding my wounded hand...
Kizutsuku te wo nandomo tsunaide

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:16.290
...you walk this uncertain path with me...
fuan bakari no kono michi wo aruite

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:29.340
...amidst the days as they slowly drift by.
yukkuri nagareta hibi no naka de bokura ga

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:41.250
The things we obtain are so warm, so beloved.
Te ni shita mono wa konna ni atatakute itoshinda

00:22:41.250 --> 00:22:47.520
Please, as time goes by, let's keep right on...
Nee konomama toki no naka

00:22:47.590 --> 00:22:52.030
...laughing and walking together.
waratte aruite yukou

00:22:52.900 --> 00:22:56.300
It's because you're with me...
Kimi ga iru kara

00:22:56.300 --> 00:23:01.400
...that I can keep moving forward.
mae ni susumerunda

00:23:02.340 --> 00:23:13.280
Now our feelings are becoming one...
Ima bokura no omoi ga hitotsu ni natte

00:23:13.590 --> 00:23:17.320
...and showing the path to us.
michi wo shimesunda

00:23:17.320 --> 00:23:21.560
So please, keep on holding my hand...
Dakara kono te zutto

00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:24.530
...and never let it go...
hanasanaide

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:27.070
LEY LINE [REIMYAKU]

00:23:27.070 --> 00:23:27.800
LEY LINE [REIMYAKU]
Ley line?

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:29.570
LEY LINE [REIMYAKU]
The path spell power flows along.

00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:30.240
LEY LINE [REIMYAKU]
If one flows to you, your business does well.

00:23:30.240 --> 00:23:31.470
If one flows to you, your business does well.

00:23:31.470 --> 00:23:32.470
Does one flow to us?

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:35.040
It does, but it seems to be
used for different things.

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:36.310
Aw, man.

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:37.880
But in return, we get some good things.

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:38.610
Right, Prof. Miwa?

00:23:38.610 --> 00:23:39.010
Next
Time
"Changeling"
Right, Prof. Miwa?

00:23:39.010 --> 00:23:40.480
Next
Time
"Changeling"
Cooking tasty rice!

